Subject: [PATCH 0023] Keep the keyboard, F11 and the frame dump working

Three faults found while exercising the stream window on the board:

- F11 was switched off while a stream ran, so the new window switching code
  could never be reached and the stream window could not be made windowed or
  fullscreen by the keyboard at all. The shortcut now stays enabled while the
  stream window exists.

- The stream window is a toplevel of its own, and the compositor focuses it when
  it maps. That quietly took the keyboard away from the interface window, which
  is the only place game input is forwarded to the host from, so WASD would have
  gone nowhere. The window asks for the focus back once it is mapped and each
  time it is focused again, and it handles F11 itself and asks the interface to
  switch the mode. Its keyboard object had only the key callback installed,
  which is not allowed: libwayland stops demarshalling the event stream at the
  first NULL callback, so the very first modifiers event desynchronised the
  connection and killed the application. All callbacks are installed now.

- The development frame dump wrote nothing and said nothing. Two reasons: a
  DMA-BUF object whose reported size is zero (ask the descriptor instead) and a
  chroma plane measured with the luma height, which made every NV12 frame look
  as if it did not fit in its object. Both fixed; anything else that goes wrong
  is reported once on stderr, and a failed write is no longer swallowed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

